Consider functions Function 1 and Function 2 expressed in pseudocode as follows:
\begin{lstlisting}
// Function 1
while n > 1 do
    for i = 1 to n do
        x = x + 1;
    end for
    n = floor(n / 2);
end while

// Function 2
for i = 1 to 100 * n do
    x = x + 1;
end for
\end{lstlisting}
Let $f_1(n)$ and $f_2(n)$ denote the number of times the statement ``$x = x + 1$'' is executed in Function 1 and Function 2, respectively.
Which of the following statements is/are TRUE?

Let $G$ be a simple, finite, undirected graph with vertex set $\{v_1, \dots, v_n\}$. Let $\Delta(G)$ denote the maximum degree of $G$ and let $\mathbb{N} = \{1, 2, \dots\}$ denote the set of all possible colors. Color the vertices of $G$ using the following greedy strategy:
\begin{lstlisting}
for i = 1, ..., n
    color(vi) <- min{j in N : no neighbour of vi is colored j}
\end{lstlisting}
Which of the following statements is/are TRUE?

